INT. HIGH SCHOOL GYMNASIUM, LOCKER ROOM - NIGHT

Rows of dented lockers. A bench running the length of the room. A whiteboard with a half-erased play: X's, O's, arrows. The score on the bell-jar scoreboard through the door: 61 - 61, 0:09 left.

COACH ISADORA PRZYBYLSKI-OKAFOR (40s, whistle, headset around her neck) paces. On the bench, in a row of damp jerseys: MARCUS "TANK" ELLISON-ADEYEMI (17, point guard), DEVON HOLLOWAY-NAKAMURA (17, forward, bag of ice on his knee), and little AMIR ZAHEDI-LINDGREN (16, bench player, towel on his head).

ISADORA
Nine seconds. Down by none.

TANK
Tied.

ISADORA
Tied is not winning.

DEVON
We know, Coach.

ISADORA
I'm talking to the bench.

AMIR
I'm on the bench.

ISADORA
I know where you are, Amir.

She taps the whiteboard. The marker squeaks.

ISADORA (CONT'D)
Tank, you inbound. Devon, you screen. Amir--

TANK
Wait, Amir's in?

DEVON
Amir's in?

AMIR
I'm in?

ISADORA
Hello, all of you. Yes. Amir's in.

TANK
Coach, with respect--

DEVON
He's never played a minute.

AMIR
Eleven minutes. In the preseason.

ISADORA
He's the only one who hasn't been guarded on tape.

TANK
That's a bad reason.

ISADORA
It's a good reason, Tank.

DEVON
What if he misses?

AMIR
What if I miss?

ISADORA
Then we go to overtime.

TANK
That's not an answer.

ISADORA
It's the only one I have.

She caps the marker. Silence. The buzzer sounds in the gym. Amir stands first, towel falling. He looks at Tank, then at Devon. Tank rises too. Devon pulls the ice off his knee, drops it in the bin, and offers Amir a fist. Amir bumps it.

ISADORA (CONT'D)
Eyes up. Hands on.

TANK
Hands on.

DEVON
Hands on.

AMIR
Hands on.

They file out. Isadora stands alone in the empty locker room. She lifts the whistle to her lips and doesn't blow.
